---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Architecture — gait">
  <main class="mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-3xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-8"><a href="/gait/docs/" class="text-sm text-[#52e5d0]">← Docs</a><article class="mt-20"><div class="eyebrow">architecture</div><h1 class="display mt-5 text-5xl font-semibold text-white">One pipeline, thin edges.</h1><p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-400">The Core is pure TypeScript. The browser package translates native events. Framework adapters only manage lifecycle and subscriptions.</p><div class="glass mt-10 rounded-3xl p-6 font-mono text-sm leading-8 text-slate-300"><div class="text-[#52e5d0]">Native browser events</div><div class="pl-5 text-slate-500">↓ normalize once</div><div class="text-[#9b8cff]">@gait/core aggregation</div><div class="pl-5 text-slate-500">↓ flush on your cadence</div><div class="text-[#f6c76b]">Versioned JSON snapshot</div></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold text-white">Performance</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">Hot paths use bounded state and online statistics. UI subscribers see snapshots, never raw pointermove events.</p></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 p-5"><h2 class="font-semibold text-white">Confidence</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">Confidence describes capture quality. It is a heuristic, not proof of a human or a device identity.</p></div></div></article></main>
</Layout>
